      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This concern touches on the core tension between accessibility and mastery in modern art. Critics of this shift argue that prioritizing opinion opens the gate to facile expression, potentially cheapening the discipline and rigor of true artistic craft. However, proponents counter that extending the definition of art allows for crucial, urgent societal conversations to take place outside the insulated world of elite skill. The \"net loss\" depends on whether one views art’s primary function as either timeless beauty or active cultural critique.",
      "source": "target",
